were $14.1&nbsp;million and $8.4&nbsp;million respectively, compared to $7.6&nbsp;million and $4.8&nbsp;million for the twelve months ended December&nbsp;31, 2023. The increase in voyage expenses is due to the increase in bunkers cost and port
expenses for the twelve months ended December&nbsp;31, 2024. The increase in vessels&#146; operating expenses is attributed to the increase in the average number of our vessels. Voyage expenses for the twelve months ended December&nbsp;31, 2024
mainly included bunker costs of $6.9&nbsp;million, corresponding to 49% of total voyage expenses, and port expenses of $4.7&nbsp;million, corresponding to 33% of total voyage expenses due to the fact that the vessel Afrapearl II operated in the spot
market. Operating expenses for the twelve months ended December&nbsp;31, 2024 mainly included crew expenses of $4.4&nbsp;million, corresponding to 52% of total operating expenses, spares and consumables costs of $1.8&nbsp;million, corresponding to
21%, and maintenance expenses of $0.9&nbsp;million, representing works and repairs on the vessels, corresponding to 11% of total vessel operating expenses. </P></TD></TR></TABLE> <P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
